        "text": "5"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "6"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "C",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Count the turns",
        "body": "From $A$ every route goes down 4 levels, each time to the lower-left or lower-right. $B$ is the second dot from the left in the bottom row, so a route to $B$ makes exactly **one** step to the right and three to the left. The right step can be the 1st, 2nd, 3rd or 4th step: 4 routes.\n\n**Answer: (C) 4**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Write numbers at the dots",
        "body": "Write at each dot the number of ways to reach it: each number is the sum of the numbers of the dots with arrows into it. Row by row: 1; 1, 1; 1, 2, 1; 1, 3, 3, 1; 1, 4, 6, 4, 1. $B$ gets 4.\n\n**Answer: (C) 4**"
      }
    ],
